- **Filesystem:** `history.sqlite3` under the DioxusLabs/Blitz data directory (apps/browser/persistence/src/lib.rs:283-285); HTTP cache at `ProjectDirs::from("com", "DioxusLabs", "Blitz").cache_dir()` on non-iOS and `$HOME/Library/Caches/http-cache` on iOS (packages/blitz-net/src/lib.rs:49-56; packages/blitz-net/src/lib.rs:44-48); screenshot default name `blitz-screenshot-<unix-secs>.<ext>` (apps/browser/src/capture.rs:103-107); `examples/output` (examples/screenshot.rs:172-173); WPT reads `WPT_DIR` and writes `output` under the parent of `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`, removing it first (wpt/runner/src/main.rs:472; wpt/runner/src/net_provider.rs:77-78; wpt/runner/src/main.rs:494-499); CI clones WPT into `./wpt/tests` and writes `./wpt/output` (.github/workflows/wpt.yml:16; .github/workflows/wpt.yml:44-51); `sites/gh-pages` Pages staging, `sites` excluded from the workspace (.github/workflows/wpt.yml:57-61; Cargo.toml:31); bundles under `./target/dx/blitz/...` (.github/workflows/publish-browser.yml:52-89); CI leg logs `target/ci-logs/{leg}.log` and `target/ci-logs/matrix-{platform}.log`, merged cargo/python output truncated at each leg's start — the only path the CI failure artifacts upload (.github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:88-89; .github/workflows/ci.yml:416-417); the coverage leg's `target/coverage/lcov.info`, uploaded on success as the `coverage-report` artifact (.github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:40-47; .github/workflows/ci.yml:286-291); the agent-run test contract's state area `target/agent-run/` — `status.json` (booted, boot time, HEAD, run state), `events.jsonl` (its JSON-line events) and `run.log` (raw merged cargo/libtest output, unscrubbed like `target/ci-logs/`, never printed) — recreated by `boot`, removed by `cleanup` with nothing else under `target/` touched, local only and uploaded by no CI job (scripts/agent-run.sh:9; scripts/agent-run.sh:165-174; scripts/agent-run.sh:215-218);
 the cold-agent pipe's state area `target/cold-agent/` — `verdict.json`, `events.jsonl`, `transcript.jsonl` (the session's raw stream-json: model output and tool I/O, unscrubbed, never printed), `client.log`, `server.log` (the escher server's stderr at `RUST_LOG=info`, counted by span name, never printed or copied) and `check.json` (the agent's check as parsed, never printed) — `calls.jsonl` and `stub-state.json` retired at 2026-10-15-cold-agent-test — recreated by `run`, removed by `cleanup` with nothing else under `target/` touched (`target/agent-run/` survives), local only and uploaded by no CI job; a per-run `mktemp -d` session directory outside the repository, holding `mcp.json` alone (the pipe copies nothing into it), removed when the run exits (scripts/cold-agent.sh:15; scripts/cold-agent.sh:450-482; scripts/cold-agent.sh:487-490); the recorded live runs' committed copies under `escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-cold-agent-run-pipe/evidence/live-*` and, since 2026-10-15-cold-agent-test, `escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-15-cold-agent-test/evidence/live-*` (`live-run.md`, `live-verdict.json`, `live-events.jsonl`, `live-check.json`, `live-transcript.jsonl`; each transcript with its host paths masked); example assets `./assets/hello_world.svg` and `./assets/servo-color-negative-no-container.png` (examples/svg.rs:4; examples/transforms.rs:3-4); the driver session's state directory — a path its caller names (the `--session <dir>` option for `escher-session`; never an env read or a cwd-relative default), created mode `0700` by `escher_driver::serve` when absent (its parent must exist) and refused as `StateDirNotPrivate` when present and open to its group or to others, holding the socket file `session.sock` alone while a session is up, and removed at `stop` or at the host's idle expiry — the socket file, then the directory by a non-recursive remove, nothing else deleted;
 the session checks' own state directories are `ss-life`, `ss-idle` and `ss-quiet` (blitz-tests) and `hb-*`, `hl-trace`, `hl-client`, `hl-client-rec`, `cc-*`, `cf-*` and `ht-timer` (seven_guis: `host_binary`, `host_log`, `cli_commands`, `cli_flow`, `host_timer`) under `CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR`, i.e. `target/tmp/`, beside the recording checks' scratch directories and escher-driver's unit tests', which reach the workspace `target/tmp` through the compile-time `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`, local only and uploaded by no CI leg (packages/escher-driver/src/host.rs:60-107; tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs:330-338; examples/seven_guis/tests/common/mod.rs:16-24; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:156; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-session/report.md, `hl-trace` at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist/report.md, the directories of the idle check and of the three command-line targets at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-driver-cli/report.md); since 2026-10-14-quality-gates escher-driver's unix-only client unit test makes one directory outside `target/tmp/`, `eab-{pid}` under the system temporary directory (`std::env::temp_dir()`), for its test-only listener, removed at the test's end — a short name, so the socket's path fits an address (packages/escher-driver/src/client.rs:263-308); observed absent — filesystem writes · searched: `std::fs|File::create|write_all` over the 15 s05 files

- **Invalidation and state integrity:** interaction state referencing a removed node is cleared or retargeted before the node is freed (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:963-1065); element-state changes take a state-only snapshot only when a rule depends on those bits (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1705-1730; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:781-786); damaged elements mark their ancestor chain (packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo.rs:1346-1350); damage propagates up the DOM and to anonymous ancestors via `layout_parent` (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:56-195); non-incremental mode marks every node `ALL_DAMAGE` (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:275-284); damage and dirty flags cleared in one visit per node, skipping clean subtrees (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:286-331); stale slab ids tolerated by `get`/`contains_key` (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:296-300; packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:527-530); `dirty_descendants` and `damaged_descendants` ancestor invariants (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:614-630; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:645-669; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_dirty_descendants.rs:5-20; tests/blitz-tests/tests/style_property_invalidation.rs:4-12); new Stylo element data marked `ALL_DAMAGE` (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/stylo_data.rs:100-105); anonymous blocks exist only in `layout_children` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_cache_invalidation.rs:1-4); every DOM mutation inserts `CONSTRUCT_BOX` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_cache_invalidation.rs:6-9); geometry memoisation invalidated by a generation counter (packages/blitz-dom/src/tree.rs:36-40; packages/blitz-dom/src/tree.rs:59-73; packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:335); animations, transitions and smooth scrolls advance via `resolve(time)` and `is_animating()` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/pseudo_element_update.rs:46-50;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/fragment_navigation.rs:31-43); a color-scheme change recascades everything (tests/blitz-tests/tests/device_coalescing.rs:94-110); reading the stylist device flushes pending changes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/device_coalescing.rs:80-92); the changed set (§Standard Contracts → Document core) is written at four kinds of site — the 15 mutation-flag sites of `DocumentMutator`, each marking the node whose in-document flag its own condition reads and only when that condition holds (the node itself in `set_node_text`, `append_text_to_node`, `set_attribute`, `clear_attribute`, `set_style_property`, `remove_style_property`, `set_sub_document`, `remove_sub_document`, `set_custom_widget`, `remove_custom_widget`, `remove_node` and `remove_and_drop_node_with`, the parent in `remove_and_drop_all_children` and `add_children_to_parent`, the moved child in `add_children_to_parent`); `snapshot_node_and` when its `ElementState` argument intersects `FOCUS` or `CHECKED`, so a focus move, a checkbox toggle and `toggle_radio` (which marks every radio of the set, changed or not); the `Input` arm of `apply_generated_text_input_event` (a typed character, an IME commit), the last two wherever the node is, in the document or not; and, since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction, `BaseDocument::apply_range_move`, which marks a range input where a key or a pointerdown changed its value and nothing for a move that changes nothing (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:333-354), and `BaseDocument::apply_select_choice`, which marks a select where a key or typeahead changed its chosen option and nothing for a choice of the chosen option (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:271-297) — and is not written by node creation, hover, active, scroll, a viewport resize, a resource load, an animation or layout, so a `resolve` with nothing written marks nothing in either layout mode;
 the set is engine-touched, a superset of what a snapshot reads as changed (an attribute re-written to itself marks and changes no reading; bounds-only movement changes a reading and marks nothing); ratified by the founder (2026-10-07), the engine half of the item §Document core records (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1716-1730; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:299-331) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff/report.md; under `accessibility` the shell rebuilds the platform accessibility tree on a poll that reported work when the changed set that poll took was non-empty — not on every document change — and takes the set on every such poll with or without the feature; ratified by the founder (2026-10-07), the shell half of the same item, its windowed witness still owed (packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:372-390); colour scheme follows the window theme with an override, default Light (packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:181-182; packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:268-272; packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:632-636)
